    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline>242 NEWPORT.<lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__754" type="place"
                            >DETROIT</rs>. 15. <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__755" type="place"
                            >Mich</rs>.<lb/><date when="1946-09-29">Sept. 29</date>.</dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof.
                        Tillich</rs>.</salute></opener>
                <p>This is to thank you for your postcard.<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note>
                    Unfortunately I cannot be in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place"
                        >New-York</rs> in the end of this month or in the beginning of October. I am
                    teaching school here like a real <unclear reason="background_noise"
                        >Schulpauker</unclear> (German and history). But if you should think it wise
                    for me to come to see you over a weekend I could easily do it.</p>
                <p>The reason and the cause for seeing you were some conversations with <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1965" type="person">Prof. Ulich</rs> and <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__710" type="person">Prof. Fr. Grant</rs>. I want to
                        <del rend="s">go to</del>
                    <add place="superlinear">teach in</add> a college if possible, <del rend="s"
                        >to</del> in a denominational college. Yet I do not know, how I could get
                    there. In <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> I had
                    studied economics and published something in this field. I was assistant to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1814" type="person">Sombart</rs> and <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__4725" type="person">Jastrow</rs>. In the meantime I
                    did not work any longer in the field of economics.<pb n="2"/></p>
                <p>Since 5 years I have been working in the field of the philosophy of history. I
                    focussed <unclear>fint</unclear> my interest on the development of the cycle
                    theory. About this problem I published two papers in the Anglican Theological
                        review.<note type="ea">Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4724" type="person"
                            >Emil Kauder</rs>: <q><rs type="work" ref="#tillich__PIFTF5XH">The
                                development of the cycle theory</rs></q> (1946); ders.: <q><rs
                                type="work" ref="#tillich__C5UTEQ4H">Ideal history: remarks on the
                                foundation of wave theory</rs></q> (1946).</note> During the last 6
                    months I am working about the collective spirit and the folksoul, I used
                    specially older German literature. Due to the lack of time (I teach 5 hours
                    daily on top of that I will be used as mixture of police dog and Prussian
                        <unclear>sergeant</unclear> against <unclear>riotous</unclear> youngsters) I
                    do not go ahead very fast with my paper. I send you my first paper, the second
                    which is in print is much better. You will get it also in due time.</p>
                <p>I am sure this is the 3815th letter of this kind <del rend="s">despite</del> you
                    have received, despite that I would be very glad if you could do anything for
                    me. Please excuse this long letter.</p>
                <closer><salute>Very sincerely,<lb/>yours</salute><signed><rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__4724" type="person">Emil
                    Kauder</rs>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
